;; no-windowserver.sb: the sandbox profile of tests/macos/macrun.py (sandbox-exec -f). It allows everything but the
;; Mach services that put a process on the desktop of the person who uses the Mac:
;;
;;   com.apple.windowserver.active          the window server (SkyLight's connection, which AppKit makes for every
;;                                          NSApplication, a window, an alert, a menu bar; CoreGraphics' session
;;                                          and display calls go through it as well)
;;   com.apple.windowmanager.server         the window manager of macOS 13 and later (Stage Manager), which AppKit
;;                                          tells about the windows of an application
;;   com.apple.dock.server                  the Dock: its tile, its icon and its menu for an application
;;   com.apple.coreservices.launchservicesd LaunchServices' check-in of an application (_RegisterApplication),
;;                                          which makes the process an application the Dock shows; an open of a
;;                                          URL or an application (NSWorkspace, open) goes there too
;;
;; The names were checked against the strings of the shared cache of macOS 26.4 (AppKit, SkyLight, HIServices,
;; LaunchServices): each of the four is there as the name of a Mach service. The other names of those families
;; that the cache holds are dispatch queues, defaults keys, notifications and files, or LaunchServices' database
;; services (com.apple.lsd.*), which put nothing on the desktop and which ordinary tools read.
;;
;; Under the profile no program can make a window or a Dock icon or show a dialog: the lookup of the window server
;; is refused, so AppKit cannot connect, and an application cannot check in. macos.sandbox.canary shows it: under
;; the profile it cannot reach the window server, and the kernel says that the process is sandboxed and that the
;; lookup is denied.

(version 1)
(allow default)
(deny mach-lookup
  (global-name "com.apple.windowserver.active")
  (global-name "com.apple.windowmanager.server")
  (global-name "com.apple.dock.server")
  (global-name "com.apple.coreservices.launchservicesd"))
